#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0236.1 expect=violation domain=TX
#note "S3 foreign discrimination (SKELETON-distinct-function hazard 3: under domain=\"TA\" the ARMCD column is TA's, not the primary TX's). The fixture adds a non-standard ARMCD column to TX so that a primary-bound read has something to read. Authority: SEND Conformance Rules v5.0 SEND236.1 (SENDIG 3.0-3.1.1, DART 1.1/1.2, GENETOX 1.0; scenario at SENDIG 3.1.1), Condition \"TXPARMCD = ARMCD\", Rule \"TXVAL is present in the TA.ARMCD\". Row 1: TXVAL=3 is not a TA.ARMCD -> fires (TX.ARMCD also says 3). Row 2: TXVAL=2 is a TA.ARMCD -> silent (TX.ARMCD says 1). A port that read ARMCD from TX would build {3, 1}: row 1 silent and row 2 firing, so the exact-set pin reds in both directions."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 SETCD=L1 TXPARMCD=ARMCD TXVAL=3
dataset TX label="Trial Sets"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col SETCD    type=Char label="Set Code"
col SET      type=Char label="Set Description"
col TXSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col TXPARMCD type=Char label="Trial Set Parameter Short Name"
col TXPARM   type=Char label="Trial Set Parameter"
col TXVAL    type=Char label="Trial Set Parameter Value"
col ARMCD    type=Char label="Planned Arm Code"
---
S1 | TX | L1 | Low Dose  | 1 | ARMCD | Planned Arm Code | 3 | 3
S1 | TX | H1 | High Dose | 2 | ARMCD | Planned Arm Code | 2 | 1
---

dataset TA label="Trial Arms"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col ARMCD   type=Char label="Planned Arm Code"
col ARM     type=Char label="Description of Planned Arm"
col TAETORD type=Num  label="Order of Element within Arm"
col ETCD    type=Char label="Element Code"
col ELEMENT type=Char label="Description of Element"
---
S1 | TA | 1 | Control   | 1 | SCRN | Screening
S1 | TA | 1 | Control   | 2 | CTRL | Vehicle Control
S1 | TA | 2 | High Dose | 1 | SCRN | Screening
S1 | TA | 2 | High Dose | 2 | HD   | 100 mg/kg
---
